"Patients — Grann Pharmaceuticals (https://www.grannpharma.com/patients)\nciteturn635search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; #### RTT-1 (Eleanor) is Grann Pharmaceuticals' investigational mRNA lipid nanoparticle (LNP) protein replacement therapy being developed for the treatment of Rett syndrome. ... #### Grann Pharmaceuticals is currently accepting inquiries from families and treating physicians who may be interested in Single-Patient Expanded Access for RTT-1 (Eleanor).\n\n#### Expanded Access is a regulatory pathway that may allow eligible patients with serious or life-threatening diseases to receive an investigational therapy outside of a clinical trial when certain medical and regulatory requirements are met.\n#### At Grann Pharmaceuticals, our patients and their families are at the heart of everything we do. We recognize the strength, resilience, and hope it takes to navigate life with Rett syndrome, and we are honored that families place their trust in us. Every conversation, every shared experience, and every patient who participates in research helps advance our understanding of Rett syndrome and brings us one step closer to developing new treatment options for children and families around the world. We are deeply grateful for your partnership and remain committed to putting patients first in everything we do.\n\n# Patients\n\n## About RTT-1 (Eleanor)\n\n#### RTT-1 (Eleanor) is Grann Pharmaceuticals' investigational mRNA lipid nanoparticle (LNP) protein replacement therapy being developed for the treatment of Rett syndrome. The therapy is designed to deliver messenger RNA (mRNA) that enables cells to produce the functional protein needed to address the underlying cause of the disease.\n\n## RTT-1 (Eleanor) Trials\n\n#### Grann Pharmaceuticals is currently accepting inquiries from families and treating physicians who may be interested in Single-Patient Expanded Access for RTT-1 (Eleanor).\n\n#### Expanded Access is a regulatory pathway that may allow eligible patients with serious or life-threatening diseases to receive an investigational therapy outside of a clinical trial when certain medical and regulatory requirements are met.\n\n#### Submitting an inquiry does not guarantee enrollment or access to RTT-1 (Eleanor), but our team is committed to carefully reviewing every request and responding as quickly as possible.\n\n## Get In Touch\n\n#### If your child has Rett syndrome and you would like to learn more about RTT-1 (Eleanor) or be considered for Single-Patient Expanded Access, we encourage you to complete the inquiry form.\n\n### Grann Pharmaceuticals\n\ninfo@grannpharma.com--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNeuCyte and Grann Pharmaceuticals Announ | NeuCyte, Inc. (https://www.neucyte.com/neucyte-and-grannpharmaceuticals-announce-strategic-partnership)\nciteturn635search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; January 13, 2026 - NeuCyte, Inc, an induced-pluripotent stem cell-based biotechnology company, today announced a strategic partnership with Grann Pharmaceuticals, Inc., a biotechnology company developing mRNA-based lipid nanoparticle (LNP) protein replacement therapies. ... (San Marcos, CA) recently completed an experimental mRNA-based treatment regimen (RTT-1) for Rett Syndrome and is advancing a growing pipeline of protein replacement therapies.\n\n# NeuCyte and Grann Pharmaceuticals Announce Strategic Partnership to Accelerate mRNA-Based Therapies for Rare Neurological Diseases\n\n​​\n\nJanuary 13, 2026 - NeuCyte, Inc, an induced-pluripotent stem cell-based biotechnology company, today announced a strategic partnership with Grann Pharmaceuticals, Inc., a biotechnology company developing mRNA-based lipid nanoparticle (LNP) protein replacement therapies. Together, the companies aim to accelerate the development and clinical translation of mRNA-based therapeutics, particularly for rare neurological diseases with high unmet need. \n\n​\n\nGrann Pharmaceuticals, Inc. (San Marcos, CA) recently completed an experimental mRNA-based treatment regimen (RTT-1) for Rett Syndrome and is advancing a growing pipeline of protein replacement therapies. Through this partnership, Grann’s mRNA-LNP delivery platform will be paired with NeuCyte’s human-relevant disease modeling capabilities to enable faster and more predictive preclinical development.\n\n​\n\nNeuCyte brings to the collaboration its New Approach Methodologies (NAMs), including patient-derived induced pluripotent stem cell (iPSC)–derived neuronal models, which are designed to establish therapeutic efficacy and accelerate pre-IND development using disease-relevant human systems. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nChiCTR2600121466 版本V1.0 版本创建时间2026/03/31 10:18:23 中国临床试验注册中心 (https://www.chictr.org.cn/hvshowproject.html?id=298322&v=1.0)\nciteturn635search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; Public title：  | A Single-Arm, Open-Label, Single-Center, Single-Dose Clinical Study Exploring the Safety and Efficacy of Intracerebroventricular Injection of RDGT-101 Injection for the Treatment of Mucopolysaccharidosis Type IIIB (MPS IIIB) ... Scientific title：  | A Single-Arm, Open-Label, Single-Center, Single-Dose Clinical Study Exploring the Safety and Efficacy of Intracerebroventricular Injection of RDGT-101 Injection for the Treatment of Mucopolysaccharidosis Type IIIB (MPS IIIB) ... The patient and/or the patient’s guardian is capable of understanding and willing to comply with the study protocol requirements and procedures, voluntarily agrees to participate, and provides signed informed consent.\nChiCTR2600121466 版本V1.0 版本创建时间2026/03/31 10:18:23 中国临床试验注册中心\n\n审核状态： Project audit state：  | 通过审核 Successful\n注册号： Registration number： [Input]  | ChiCTR2600121466 \n最近更新日期： Date of Last Refreshed on：  | 2026-03-31 10:18:04 \n注册时间： Date of Registration：  | 2026-03-31 00:00:00 \n注